Share native members through lazy tree mappings

Native transport should preserve shared relation suffixes when member
images follow an increasing partial map. Carry compressed offset runs
through prefix keys and suffix values, compose compatible offsets, and
cache transformed children only when they are visited.

Keep small materialized relations eager and merge non-injective images
into owned destination suffixes. Represent dense leaves as intervals
and retain persistent interval trees when equality introduces holes.
Consume incoming suffixes during insertion so fresh pivots stay unique
through recursive unions instead of being copied again.

Preserve canonical current rows, historical snapshots, and finite fuel
through equality and updates. Keep cache coordinates tied to their raw
source and release deep mapping chains without recursive stack growth.
Use partial domains only to choose comparison lookups; leave stored
bounds and eager-mapping thresholds unchanged. Equivalent partial
views still skip their shared source without visiting individual keys.

Keep ordinary nodes compact, update only edited paths, and build
sorted levels without repeated searches. Specialize exact-tree updates
to skip deferred-node checks and adjust known counts directly. Keep
the small balance check inline while resolving rotations in a separate
helper. Reuse target coverage during ownership cleanup and share
transport map deltas only when both current and previous snapshots
match.

Regression coverage includes native and desugared evaluators under
both evaluation strategies, randomized mutation sequences, filtered
pivots, partial and conflicting images, noncanonical rows, source and
owner equalities, shared snapshots, deep chains, late images, and
finite fuel.

Record native CGU16 measurements against f29c6e6. Dense consumption
improves substantially; sparse incremental and equality controls still
have measurable overhead. Preserve the exact methodology and hashes.

Lazy caches and stack-safe destruction tighten the generic WBTreeMap
lifetime behavior: previous covariance and some early-dropping
borrowed value examples are not preserved. Generated evaluators use
owned values.

Extend inherited secondary indices with newly projected owned rows.
The previous owned seed is already present, so unioning it again after
every local rule firing revisited all preceding owners in an acyclic
chain.

Prepare arithmetic image blocks directly so compact namespaces can map
shared trees without allocating an explicit tuple for every image.
Preserve sparse relation sharing when these prepared maps request a
deferred view instead of materializing small suffixes at every owner.

Introduce persistent member domains and scoped equality partitions
over stable origins. Virtual handle blocks preserve separate owner
identities without allocating every inherited image. Refresh shares
source state and replays local constraints while historical snapshots
remain stable. Keep old handles valid on explicit adoption, reserve
sparse weights without filling virtual slots, and provide native
member root masks.

Identify equivalent prepared column transforms independently of their
value caches. Shared source subtrees can then cancel during
comparisons and set operations without forcing every inherited suffix.

Keep late image changes in whole transported suffixes. Merge
destination paths once per changed member column, while earlier stable
column maps retain the existing attribution of simultaneous changes.
Sparse nonmonotone head maps use direct source lookups instead of
scanning unrelated rows.

Track origin-row incidence so equality rewrites visit only the losing
representative's rows. Parent relation snapshots and historical owner
states keep sharing unaffected structure.

Rebase selected owner indexes by sharing current parent roots. Replay
only local support and local equality merges. Revision checkpoints
avoid repeating unchanged rebases while persistent snapshots preserve
history.

Expose ordered local quotient changes so owner rebases can share
source rows and then apply only their local equations.

Preserve member handles through materialization without making
reserved namespace holes into elements. Maintain compact canonical
domains and export their actual carriers and aliases through dynamic
model data.

Connect scoped native member operations to compact identity spaces.
Convert local origin outputs back to owner handles on mutation.
Preserve public root and allocation behavior.

Retain local quotient events when only parent rows change, so
inherited row refresh still respects equations already made in the
target.

Feed native owner scopes from shared origin indexes. Rebase inherited
roots and replay local support without building explicit image tuples.

Execute compact scoped rules through late source growth, local
equations, reverse function lookups, and owner-local member
enumeration.

Reject compact activation when member coordinates can escape their owner
scope. Validate selected indexes and scheduled rule scopes. Allow
member-free global relations and generated morphism rules.

Translate compact origin rows at public query boundaries. Preserve
owner-local handles, alias-aware membership, and lazy row iteration
without expanding inherited tables for point lookups.

Freeze scoped output handles before applying mutations. A change of
storage during equality must not reinterpret pending origin values.
